id: pm-5bsofk
title: "GH-1218: expose local package copy scope and packed-install alternatives"
description: Expose a bounded machine-readable local-directory copy-cost plan and a verified packed-install alternative without silently changing directory snapshot semantics.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-07T22:30:37.538Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-08T21:02:26.071Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-08T20:41:36.422Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-08T20:41:36.422Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "SDK and CLI local-source planning identifies directory versus archive source and bounded file/byte estimates before copying; large development trees receive a working npm pack and archive-install suggestion; preserve directory snapshots, ignored scripts, dependency resolution, containment and exact host SDK linking; real isolated directory and archive acceptance covers the published consumer flow."
parent: pm-ugqx
risk: medium
confidence: high
release: 2026.9.8
reporter: github
severity: medium
resolution: "Implemented bounded SDK/CLI/MCP copy planning and safe archive alternatives, with real packed-install acceptance now using the existing Windows npm launcher helpers."
expected_result: "Directory and archive planning retain their existing semantics, and the same real pack/install acceptance runs on supported operating systems."
actual_result: "All 8620 tests pass at exact 100/100/100/100 coverage. All three linked package commands, four TypeScript projects and static assurance pass. Linux and macOS hosted suites passed; the corrected-head Windows run remains a merge requirement. The original feature remains attributed to v2026.9.8."
